        "ExplanationWrongB": "Cycle time is an internal operational metric, not a direct customer-facing measure. Customer measures in the BSC include customer satisfaction scores, on-time delivery percentage, market share, and customer retention rates. While cycle time reduction may improve customer satisfaction indirectly, the metric itself tracks internal process efficiency.",
        "ExplanationWrongC": "",
        "ExplanationWrongD": "While cycle time improvement may require employee training and skill development, cycle time itself measures operational process efficiency, not workforce capability. Learning and Growth measures include employee turnover rate, training hours per employee, skill certification rates, and employee satisfaction. These are input drivers that enable better processes, but cycle time is the process outcome itself.",
