        "ExplanationCorrect": "The control environment is the foundation of the COSO internal control framework and sets the tone of an organization, influencing the control consciousness of its people. It includes factors such as integrity and ethical values, commitment to competence, board of directors and audit committee participation, management's philosophy and operating style, organizational structure, assignment of authority and responsibility, and human resource policies and practices. When the CEO explicitly prioritizes results over process ('results justify the approach') and the organization rewards employees who meet targets regardless of compliance concerns, the control environment is fundamentally weakened. The control environment is the most directly affected component because it reflects the tone at the top — the ethical climate and behavioral expectations set by senior management and the board. A strong control environment is a prerequisite for the other four COSO components (risk assessment, control activities, information and communication, and monitoring) to function effectively. Without an appropriate tone at the top, even well-designed control activities may be overridden or ignored.",
